  "description": "ZEWLUK crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: H4 N1 1+,C160 H184 Er9 O42 1-. From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 10 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er5 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2A (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3A (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er4A (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er5A (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.525-5.075 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 84.03-169.38°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula NH4[Er9(L)16(μ3-OH)8(μ5-O)2](H2O)3. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ5-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
